{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_0b3ab8e4cbbbce424f0742d37d87b2be35c3a374c51347c8f3248f96c8f3c00f", "title": "Entre Ríos Province", "text": "Entre Ríos (] , \"Between Rivers\") is a central province of Argentina, located in the Mesopotamia region. It borders the provinces of Buenos Aires (south), Corrientes (north) and Santa Fe (west), and Uruguay in the east.", "score": 22.0466}, {"id": "hp_doc_e7f1d75a2e8642ecb6004ef5be21eba203458a6c1f8ff63b2f3f3320cc442645", "title": "Puerto Ibicuy", "text": "Puerto Ibicuy is a village and municipality in Entre Ríos Province in north-eastern Argentina.", "score": 20.6617}, {"id": "hp_doc_c49dc7e1c09feabd3bea9a32de202cea9fffd508f6588b54c358fbbc56c668ee", "title": "Gualeguay River", "text": "The Gualeguay River (Spanish Río Gualeguay) is one of the major rivers of the Mesopotamic province of Entre Ríos, Argentina. Its source is in the north of the province, in the region between the cities of Federación and San José de Feliciano, and meanders in a general south-southwestward direction across the center of the province for about 350 to , receiving a large number of tributary streams. It passes by the cities of Villaguay, Rosario del Tala, and Gualeguay, and finally empties into the Río Paraná Ibicuy, a distributary of the Paraná River in the Paraná Delta.", "score": 15.519}], "remaining_searches": 1}
